  "description": "Diamond is pure carbon, like pencil graphite, but with its atoms in a very strong 3D network. Natural diamonds form about 150 km deep under huge pressure and over 1,000 °C; many are 1 to 3.5 billion years old and rise in deep kimberlite eruptions. They're the hardest natural material, and the white dwarf BPM 37093 ('Lucy') has a crystallized carbon core. Original 3D animation; not to scale.",
